# XSH sched_getparam()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# A negative pid is unspecified and not tested. Which processes the caller
# may query is implementation-defined, so EPERM is not provoked; the
# other-process test runs privileged and treats a refusal as UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XSH.sched_getparam.001
anchor     functions/sched_getparam.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/sched_getparam.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       PS
since      2001
says       sched_getparam(0, &sp) returns 0 and stores a priority that lies
           within the range sched_get_priority_min()/max() give for the
           caller's current policy.
note       UNRESOLVED if the policy has no range to compare with, or a
           bound comes back as -1 (the failure value; it cannot be told
           from a failed call whose errno was not set).
test       t/001-self.c

assertion  XSH.sched_getparam.002
anchor     functions/sched_getparam.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       PS
since      2001
says       sched_getparam(getpid(), ...) returns 0 and the same priority as
           sched_getparam(0, ...).
test       t/002-own-pid.c

assertion  XSH.sched_getparam.003
anchor     functions/sched_getparam.html#ERRORS/ESRCH
anchor     functions/sched_getparam.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       PS
since      2001
says       For the pid of a child that has been reaped, sched_getparam()
           returns -1 with ESRCH.
test       t/003-esrch.c

assertion  XSH.sched_getparam.004
anchor     functions/sched_getparam.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       PS
since      2001
says       sched_getparam(pid, ...) of another existing process returns that
           process's priority (a child under SCHED_FIFO with a chosen
           priority), not the caller's.
needs      root
timeout    60
test       t/004-other-process.c
